# No unrequested pull requests (Cursor agents)

Never create, push-to-open, or update a pull request unless the user **explicitly** asked to do that in this turn.

## Off-limits without an explicit ask

- `gh pr create`, `gh pr edit`, `gh pr merge`
- Cursor / MCP `create_pull_request` (or equivalent)
- `git push -u` whose purpose is to enable or open a PR
- Filling in a PR body, title, closing keywords, or screenshots **on GitHub**

## Never treat these as PR permission

- Implementing or “building” a plan
- Tests passing, issue definition of done, or “closes #n” in an issue/plan
- “Done”, “ship it”, or leftover docs/copy polish
- The user saying they will open the PR, or that a PR already exists

Drafting a title/body **in chat** is fine when asked. Creating the PR is not.

Related: [no-unrequested-commits.mdc](no-unrequested-commits.mdc). Do not remove or narrow this rule unless the user asked (see [no-unrequested-deletions.mdc](no-unrequested-deletions.mdc)).
